WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.559
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:09.396
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:14.891
Unit eleven: Last Weekend. In this unit, you will talk about what you did last weekend.

4
00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:16.687
Weekend.

5
00:00:17.387 --> 00:00:19.410
Weekend means Saturday and Sunday.

6
00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.709
I visited my cousins at the weekend.

7
00:00:22.409 --> 00:00:24.980
Your turn. Say: Weekend.

8
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:28.484
Weekend.

9
00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:30.217
Visited.

10
00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:35.111
Visited means past of visit: went to see someone or somewhere.

11
00:00:35.411 --> 00:00:36.784
We visited the zoo.

12
00:00:37.484 --> 00:00:40.334
Your turn. Say: Visited.

13
00:00:43.034 --> 00:00:43.965
Visited.

14
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:45.800
Watched.

15
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.974
Watched means past of watch: looked at something for a time.

16
00:00:50.274 --> 00:00:51.925
We watched a funny film.

17
00:00:52.625 --> 00:00:54.825
Your turn. Say: Watched.

18
00:00:57.525 --> 00:00:58.340
Watched.

19
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:00.107
Played.

20
00:01:00.807 --> 00:01:03.434
Played means past of play: had fun with a game.

21
00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.617
I played football with my cousins.

22
00:01:06.317 --> 00:01:08.447
Your turn. Say: Played.

23
00:01:11.147 --> 00:01:11.881
Played.

24
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:13.641
Went.

25
00:01:14.341 --> 00:01:17.582
Went means past of go: moved to a place.

26
00:01:17.882 --> 00:01:19.151
We went to the market.

27
00:01:19.851 --> 00:01:21.818
Your turn. Say: Went.

28
00:01:24.518 --> 00:01:25.264
Went.

29
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:26.914
Ate.

30
00:01:27.614 --> 00:01:29.788
Ate means past of eat: had food.

31
00:01:30.088 --> 00:01:31.426
I ate noodle soup.

32
00:01:32.126 --> 00:01:34.418
Your turn. Say: Ate.

33
00:01:37.118 --> 00:01:37.829
Ate.

34
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:39.516
Saw.

35
00:01:40.216 --> 00:01:43.330
Saw means past of see: used your eyes.

36
00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:45.130
We saw a big elephant.

37
00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.819
Your turn. Say: Saw.

38
00:01:51.519 --> 00:01:52.416
Saw.

39
00:01:53.417 --> 00:01:54.441
Yesterday.

40
00:01:55.141 --> 00:01:57.175
Yesterday means the day before today.

41
00:01:57.475 --> 00:01:58.906
Yesterday was Sunday.

42
00:01:59.606 --> 00:02:02.456
Your turn. Say: Yesterday.

43
00:02:05.156 --> 00:02:06.250
Yesterday.

44
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.308
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:09.608 --> 00:02:12.304
Sreypich, what did you do last weekend?

46
00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:15.639
I visited my cousins in Takeo.

47
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:17.986
What did you do there?

48
00:02:19.283 --> 00:02:21.469
We played football and watched a film.

49
00:02:22.783 --> 00:02:24.411
Did you go out on Sunday?

50
00:02:25.717 --> 00:02:28.552
Yes, we went to the market and ate noodle soup.

51
00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:33.405
Grammar focus: Past simple (regular and irregular).

52
00:02:33.705 --> 00:02:35.986
I played football. We went to the market.

53
00:02:36.286 --> 00:02:40.445
Learn irregular verbs in pairs: go–went, eat–ate, see–saw, have–had.

54
00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:44.590
Now read and listen. A Weekend with My Cousins.

55
00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.435
Last weekend, I visited my cousins in Takeo.

56
00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:52.305
On Saturday, we played football in the field and watched a film at night.

57
00:02:53.617 --> 00:02:56.533
On Sunday, we went to the market and ate noodle soup.

58
00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:00.418
We also saw a big buffalo near the river.

59
00:03:01.717 --> 00:03:04.703
Yesterday, I was tired, but I was very happy!

60
00:03:06.017 --> 00:03:08.623
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:08.923 --> 00:03:10.957
Last Sunday, we blank to the market.

62
00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:14.492
A, go. B, went. C, goed.

63
00:03:18.483 --> 00:03:19.914
The answer is B: went.

64
00:03:21.417 --> 00:03:23.335
I blank noodle soup for lunch.

65
00:03:23.635 --> 00:03:26.360
A, eat. B, ate. C, eated.

66
00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.384
The answer is B: ate.

67
00:03:33.883 --> 00:03:36.429
The day before today is blank.

68
00:03:36.729 --> 00:03:40.161
A, yesterday. B, tomorrow. C, weekend.

69
00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.150
The answer is A: yesterday.

70
00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:50.674
Now it's your turn to speak. What did you do last weekend?

71
00:03:55.974 --> 00:04:03.305
Last weekend, I helped my mother at home, and then I played badminton with my friends. On Sunday, we went to the park.

72
00:04:03.605 --> 00:04:05.175
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:06.183 --> 00:04:11.123
Great work today! You learned eight new words and past simple (regular and irregular).

74
00:04:11.423 --> 00:04:14.412
Today's value is family. Love and help your family.

75
00:04:14.712 --> 00:04:17.283
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

76
00:04:17.583 --> 00:04:20.270
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

